QUESTIONS = json.loads('[{"n":1,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t10","stem":"Let X be the random variable with PDF f_X(x)=1/2 for 0<x<2 and 0 otherwise. Then the PDF of Y=\\u221aX is:","answer":"A","explanation":"The transformation is increasing: x=y\\u00b2 and dx/dy=2y. Thus f_Y(y)=f_X(y\\u00b2)|dx/dy|=(1/2)(2y)=y on 0<y<\\u221a2; it is zero elsewhere.","options":["f_Y(y)=y for 0<y\\u2264\\u221a2, and 0 otherwise.","f_Y(y)=y\\u00b2 for 0<y<\\u221a2, and 0 otherwise.","f_Y(y)=y for 0<y<1, and 0 otherwise.","f_Y(y)=1 for 0<y\\u22641, and 0 otherwise."]},{"n":4,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t7","stem":"Let a random variable X have mean \\u03bc=10 and variance \\u03c3\\u00b2=4. Using Chebyshev\'s inequality, which value of c does not guarantee that P(|X\\u221210|>c)\\u22640.04?","answer":"D","explanation":"Chebyshev gives P(|X\\u2212\\u03bc|>c)\\u22644/c\\u00b2. To make this at most 0.04 requires c\\u00b2\\u2265100, or c\\u226510. The value 8 does not ensure the bound.","options":["10","21","12","8"]},{"n":5,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t7","stem":"Let a random variable X have mean \\u03bc=8 and variance \\u03c3\\u00b2=9. If P(|X\\u22128|>6)\\u2264U, then U is:","answer":"C","explanation":"Chebyshev\'s inequality gives P(|X\\u2212\\u03bc|>c)\\u2264\\u03c3\\u00b2/c\\u00b2. Here U=9/6\\u00b2=1/4.","options":["1/2","1/3","1/4","4/3"]},{"n":6,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t7","stem":"A random variable X has a Poisson distribution with parameter 9. The upper bound for P(X\\u226515) is:","answer":"A","explanation":"Since X is nonnegative, Markov\'s inequality gives P(X\\u226515)\\u2264E[X]/15=9/15=3/5.","options":["3/5","4/3","1/36","35/36"]},{"n":7,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t7","stem":"The mean and standard deviation of pony weights in a large animal shelter are 20 kg and 3 kg. A pony is selected at random. Using Chebyshev\'s inequality, the lower bound for the probability that its weight is between 14 kg and 26 kg is:","answer":"D","explanation":"The interval is |X\\u221220|<6, which is within 2 standard deviations because 6/3=2. Chebyshev gives P(|X\\u2212\\u03bc|<2\\u03c3)\\u22651\\u22121/2\\u00b2=3/4.","options":["3/7","4/7","0","3/4"]},{"n":8,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t7","stem":"Let X\\u223cU(0,1). Which statement is NOT correct?","answer":"B","explanation":"For a uniform variable on (0,1), E(X\\u00b2)=\\u222b\\u2080\\u00b9x\\u00b2dx=1/3, which is less than 1/2. Thus (b) is the false statement. The other inequalities follow from Jensen\'s inequality and concavity or convexity.","options":["E[ln(1+X)]\\u2264ln(3/2)","E(X\\u00b2)\\u22651/2","E(e^X)\\u2265e^(1/2)","E(\\u221aX)\\u22641/\\u221a2"]},{"n":9,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t7","stem":"Let X have distribution function F(x)=1\\u2212e^(\\u2212x/10), x\\u22650. Which is a valid lower bound for E(e^[1/(1+X)])?","answer":"B","explanation":"This is an exponential distribution with mean 10. The function 1/(1+x) is convex for x\\u22650, so Jensen gives E[1/(1+X)]\\u22651/(1+E[X])=1/11. Applying the increasing convex exponential gives E[e^(1/(1+X))]\\u2265e^(E[1/(1+X)])\\u2265e^(1/11).","options":["e^(\\u221210)","e^(1/11)","e^(\\u221211)","e^(1/10)"]},{"n":10,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"If X is a random variable with PDF f(x)=k/(1+x)^3 for 0<x<\\u221e and 0 otherwise, which statement is true?","answer":"B","explanation":"Normalization requires k\\u222b\\u2080\\u221e(1+x)\\u207b\\u00b3dx=1. The integral is 1/2, so k=2. The second-moment integrand behaves like 2/x for large x, so E[X\\u00b2] diverges and the variance is infinite.","options":["k=3, Var(X)=\\u221e","k=2, Var(X)=\\u221e","k=3, Var(X)<\\u221e","k=2, Var(X)<\\u221e"]},{"n":11,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t10","stem":"The random variable X has PDF f(x)=(3/2)x\\u00b2 for \\u22121<x<1 and 0 otherwise. What are E(|X|) and Var(|X|), respectively?","answer":"D","explanation":"By symmetry, E|X|=2\\u222b\\u2080\\u00b9x(3x\\u00b2/2)dx=3/4. Also E(|X|\\u00b2)=E(X\\u00b2)=2\\u222b\\u2080\\u00b9x\\u00b2(3x\\u00b2/2)dx=3/5. Therefore Var(|X|)=3/5\\u2212(3/4)\\u00b2=3/80.","options":["1/4, 1/80","3/4, 1/80","1/4, 3/80","3/4, 3/80"]},{"n":12,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t5","stem":"Let X have PMF P(X=x)=e^(\\u2212\\u03bb)\\u03bb^x/x!, x=0,1,2,\\u2026 . Find P(10^X>1) if \\u03bb=1.","answer":"C","explanation":"Because X is a nonnegative integer, 10^X>1 exactly when X>0. For a Poisson(1) variable, P(X>0)=1\\u2212P(X=0)=1\\u2212e\\u207b\\u00b9=(e\\u22121)/e.","options":["e/(e+1)","(1/2)(1\\u2212e)","(e\\u22121)/e","1/e"]},{"n":13,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t5","stem":"Let X and Y be independent random variables with X\\u223cBin(5,1/2) and Y\\u223cPoisson(5). If Z=0.4X+0.6Y, then Var(Z) is:","answer":"A","explanation":"Independence gives Var(Z)=0.4\\u00b2Var(X)+0.6\\u00b2Var(Y). The variances are 5(1/2)(1/2)=5/4 and 5, so Var(Z)=0.16(1.25)+0.36(5)=0.2+1.8=2.","options":["2","1.5","1","2.5"]},{"n":14,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"If the density of a continuous random variable X is f(x)=ax for 0\\u2264x\\u22641, a for 1\\u2264x\\u22642, a(3\\u2212x) for 2\\u2264x\\u22643, and 0 elsewhere, find P(X>1.5).","answer":"B","explanation":"The total area is a/2+a+a/2=2a, so a=1/2. Integrating from 1.5 to 2 gives 1/4, and from 2 to 3 the triangular area is 1/4. The total tail probability is 1/2.","options":["1/3","1/2","1/4","3/2"]},{"n":15,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"Let X have distribution function F(x)=0 for x<0; 2x/5 for 0\\u2264x<1; 3/5 for 1\\u2264x<2; x/2+1/8 for 2\\u2264x<3; and 1 for x\\u22653. Then P(2\\u2264X<4) is:","answer":"D","explanation":"There is no probability above 3, so P(2\\u2264X<4)=P(X\\u22652)=1\\u2212F(2\\u2212). The left limit at 2 is 3/5, giving 2/5.","options":["4/5","1/4","1/5","2/5"]},{"n":16,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"Which of the following is a valid PDF? (a) f(x)=x for 0<x<1, zero otherwise. (b) f(x)=(3/4)(1\\u2212x\\u00b2) for \\u22121<x<1, zero otherwise. (c) f(x)=8x\\u00b2 for 0<x<2, zero otherwise. (d) f(x)=(4/3)(1+x\\u00b2) for \\u22121<x<1, zero otherwise.","answer":"B","explanation":"A density must be nonnegative and integrate to one. Option (b) is nonnegative on (\\u22121,1), and its integral is (3/4)[x\\u2212x\\u00b3/3] from \\u22121 to 1, equal to 1. The other options do not integrate to 1.","options":["(a)","(b)","(c)","(d)"]},{"n":17,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"Let X have PDF f(x)=(x/8)e^(\\u2212x\\u00b2/16) for x\\u22650 and 0 otherwise. What is the median of X?","answer":"D","explanation":"Integrating the density gives F(x)=1\\u2212e^(\\u2212x\\u00b2/16). Set F(m)=1/2: e^(\\u2212m\\u00b2/16)=1/2, so m\\u00b2=16 ln 2 and m=4\\u221a(ln 2).","options":["2\\u221a(ln 2)","2\\u221a(ln 4)","\\u221a(ln 2)","4\\u221a(ln 2)"]},{"n":18,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t4","stem":"Suppose X has PDF f(x)=896/x^8 for x\\u22652 and 0 otherwise. What is the highest moment of X that exists?","answer":"C","explanation":"The rth raw moment has tail proportional to \\u222b\\u2082\\u221ex^(r\\u22128)dx. It converges when r\\u22128<\\u22121, or r<7. The highest integer order that exists is 6.","options":["4","5","6","7"]},{"n":19,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t2","stem":"A line of length l is divided into two equal parts. If the first part has length X, find E(e^X | X<l/2).","answer":"B","explanation":"A uniformly chosen point gives X\\u223cU(0,l). Conditional on X<l/2, X is uniform on (0,l/2). Hence the conditional expectation is (2/l)\\u222b\\u2080^(l/2)e^x dx=(2/l)(e^(l/2)\\u22121).","options":["(2/l)(e^l\\u22121)","(2/l)(e^(l/2)\\u22121)","(2/l)(e^(l/2)+1)","(2/l)(e^l+1)"]},{"n":23,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t4","stem":"Find the moment generating function of X if its PDF is f(x)=x for 0<x<1, f(x)=2\\u2212x for 1<x<2, and 0 otherwise.","answer":"B","explanation":"This triangular density is the distribution of the sum of two independent U(0,1) variables. A U(0,1) variable has MGF (e^t\\u22121)/t, and independent MGFs multiply, giving ((e^t\\u22121)/t)^2.","options":["((e^t\\u2212e^(\\u2212t))/t)^2","((e^t\\u22121)/t)^2","((e^(2t)\\u22121)/t)^2","None of these"]},{"n":24,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t4","stem":"Let X be a random variable with moment generating function M_X(t)=(1/16)(3+e^t)^2, t\\u2208R. If Y=2^X, find E[Y(Y+1)].","answer":"C","explanation":"Since Y(Y+1)=2^(2X)+2^X, its expectation is M_X(ln 4)+M_X(ln 2). These are (3+4)^2/16=49/16 and (3+2)^2/16=25/16; their sum is 74/16=37/8.","options":["49/16","37/16","37/8","25/16"]},{"n":26,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"Let X be a continuous random variable with PDF f(x) = 1/8 for 2 \\u2264 x \\u2264 10, and 0 otherwise. What is the distribution of Y = aX + b, provided a > 0?","answer":"B","explanation":"X is uniform on [2, 10]. Since a > 0, the transformation Y = aX + b preserves endpoint order: 2 maps to 2a + b and 10 maps to 10a + b. Thus Y is uniform on [2a + b, 10a + b], option (b).","options":["U(8a + b, 12a + b)","U(2a + b, 10a + b)","Poisson(ba/8)","None of the above"]},{"n":27,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t2","stem":"A random variable X has distribution f(x) = 1/12 for 0 < x < 12, and 0 otherwise. What is P(5 < X < 7 | X > 6)?","answer":"D","explanation":"Given X > 6, the conditioning interval is (6, 12), of length 6. The event 5 < X < 7 within it is (6, 7), of length 1. Uniformity gives the conditional probability 1/6, option (d).","options":["1/3","4/3","3/2","1/6"]},{"n":28,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t6","stem":"Let k > 0 be a constant such that the PDF of X is f(x) = kx(1 \\u2212 x) for 0 < x < 1, and 0 elsewhere. What is the value of the harmonic mean of X?","answer":"D","explanation":"Normalizing gives k\\u222b\\u2080\\u00b9x(1 \\u2212 x)dx = k/6 = 1, so k = 6. Then E(1/X) = \\u222b\\u2080\\u00b9(1/x)6x(1 \\u2212 x)dx = 6\\u222b\\u2080\\u00b9(1 \\u2212 x)dx = 3. The harmonic mean is 1/E(1/X) = 1/3, option (d).","options":["1/2","1/4","1/6","1/3"]},{"n":29,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t5","stem":"Let X be a Poisson random variable with parameter \\u03bb such that P(X = 2) = 2P(X = 4) + 20P(X = 6). What is the coefficient of skewness?","answer":"A","explanation":"Substitute the Poisson probabilities and cancel e^(\\u2212\\u03bb)\\u03bb\\u00b2: 1/2 = \\u03bb\\u00b2/12 + \\u03bb\\u2074/36. With t = \\u03bb\\u00b2, this gives t\\u00b2 + 3t \\u2212 18 = 0, so t = 3 since \\u03bb > 0. Thus \\u03bb = \\u221a3. A Poisson variable has skewness 1/\\u221a\\u03bb, giving 1/\\u221a(\\u221a3), option (a).","options":["1/\\u221a(\\u221a3)","1/\\u221a(1/\\u221a3)","1/\\u221a3","1/3"]},{"n":30,"format":"single","module":"probability","topic":"probability-t5","stem":"Let X be a discrete random variable with PMF P(X = x) = (2x + 3)/21 for x = 1, 2, 3, and 0 otherwise. If I\\u2096 = 1 when X \\u2265 k and 0 when X < k, and Z = I\\u2081 + I\\u2082 + I\\u2083, then find E(Z).","answer":"C","explanation":"By linearity, E(Z) = \\u03a3\\u2096\\u208c\\u2081\\u00b3P(X \\u2265 k). The three tail probabilities are 1, 16/21, and 9/21, so E(Z) = 1 + 16/21 + 9/21 = 46/21, option (c).","options":["56/21","16/21","46/21","19/3"]}]')


def build():
    out = {m: [] for m in OUTS}
    for q in QUESTIONS:
        iid, ref = "topic-wise-test-series-1-q%03d" % q["n"], LABEL + ", Q%d" % q["n"]
        if q["format"] == "single":
            it = S(iid, q["module"], q["topic"], ref, q["stem"], q["options"], q["answer"], q["explanation"])
        elif q["format"] == "multi":
            it = M(iid, q["module"], q["topic"], ref, q["stem"], q["statements"], q["answer"], q["whys"], "ABCD"[(q["n"] - 1) % 4], q["explanation"])
        else:
            it = N(iid, q["module"], q["topic"], ref, q["stem"], q["answer"], q["explanation"], q["check"])
        out[q["module"]].append(it["item"])
    return {m: {"moduleId": m, "source": "variant", "label": LABEL, "count": len(items), "items": items} for m, items in out.items()}


def main():
    built = build()
    for module, rel in OUTS.items():
        target = os.path.join(ROOT, rel)
        text = json.dumps(built[module], ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + "\n"
        if "--check" in sys.argv:
            with open(target, encoding="utf-8") as f:
                if f.read() != text:
                    raise SystemExit(rel + " differs; run python topic_wise_test_series_1_bank.py")
        else:
            with open(target, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n") as f:
                f.write(text)
        print(rel + ": " + str(built[module]["count"]) + " items")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
